# ENSO — Environment variables
#
# ENSO is a Supabase-backed app: auth, subscriptions, payments and budgets are
# all stored in Supabase (Postgres + Auth), NOT in a local browser database.
# Without these variables the app builds, but auth and data sync will not work
# (the client silently falls back to disabled/placeholder credentials).
#
# --- Setup steps ---
# 1. Create a free project at https://supabase.com
# 2. Go to Project Settings > API and copy the "Project URL" and "anon public" key below.
# 3. Run the SQL migration in supabase/migrations/001_initial_schema.sql
#    (Supabase Dashboard > SQL Editor > paste and run), this creates the
#    `subscriptions`, `payments` and `budgets` tables + Row Level Security policies.
# 4. Go to Authentication > Providers and enable "Email".
#    Optionally enable Google / GitHub if you want social login.
# 5. Go to Authentication > URL Configuration and add your app's callback URL
#    as an allowed Redirect URL, e.g.:
#      http://localhost:3000/auth/callback        (development)
#      https://your-domain.com/auth/callback      (production)
# 6. Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values below.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
